From 5ee0385bfc2eac33d6b791a1b3eaac9f6305e994 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:46:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Redesign board UI as a dense, keyboard-first tool

Rework the visual design around density and structure instead of
floating cards:

- Replace shadows/large radii with hairline rails; task cards become
  rows on a continuous surface. Top bar 80px -> 48px, sidebar
  261px -> 220px.
- Drop per-column accent hues. Colour is reserved for one signal
  accent meaning active progress; columns are identified by position
  and label.
- Completed tasks recede (secondary text + check glyph, no meter) so
  contrast is spent on work that still needs attention.
- Move all themed colours to CSS variables consumed through Tailwind
  tokens, replacing raw hex scattered across components.
- Add working keyboard bindings with hints rendered only where a
  binding exists: mod+1..9 switches boards, N opens a new task,
  Esc closes overlays. Bindings are ignored while typing in a field.

Fixes carried over from the prior pass:

- Task title and subtask counter rendered as adjacent inline spans and
  ran together ("Build UI for onboarding flow1 of 3").
- Column dot colours used shuffle().pop() in an effect, re-rolling on
  every mount and letting neighbouring columns collide.
- "+ New column" was clipped off the right edge.
- Sidebar board icons were forced white by a filter and vanished
  against the light sidebar; now inline SVG using currentColor.
- TaskModal rendered DeleteModal without setIsDeleteModalOpen, so
  dismissing a task-delete confirm threw.
- Board columns collapsed to zero width at mobile widths (missing
  flex shrink-0).
- Replaced a window-resize listener that re-subscribed on every render
  with CSS breakpoints.

Text colours in both themes now meet WCAG AA (5.0-18:1); the dimmest
token is used only for keyboard chips, where the 3:1 UI threshold
applies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
