From 8daed801091da7e9ab19c576477dceaf0c43e0b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:54:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Persist boards to localStorage and add per-task time
 tracking

Persistence:

Board state was rebuilt from src/data/data.json on every page load, so
edits and deletions reappeared on refresh. The store now hydrates from
localStorage when a saved value exists and falls back to the seed on a
first visit. Writes are coalesced on a 150ms timer because dragging and
ticking subtasks dispatch in bursts. Every storage access is wrapped:
localStorage throws in private mode and when site data is blocked, and
that must not stop the app rendering.

Time tracking:

Tasks gain two optional fields, timeSpent (banked ms) and startedAt
(epoch ms of the run in progress), so existing data keeps working.
Only one task runs at a time; starting another banks the previous one.
`now` is passed into the reducers so they stay pure.

- Hover a task row for a start/stop control; elapsed time stays visible
  once a task has any, and counts live while running.
- A running task keeps its accent edge pinned rather than on hover.
- The task panel gains a clock with Start/Stop and Reset.
- The header shows a global running indicator that doubles as a stop
  button, so a timer running on another board stays visible.
- useTicker only registers an interval while something is running.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014dtmom2BFbpLMj9Na8hSrG
