From 36c1cbacd0735a68401aad11992df345d2ada266 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:08:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Auto-start the timer on task creation and add due dates

Timer:

Creating a task now starts its clock immediately. Because only one task
is ever on the clock, creating one banks whatever was running. The
control is a pause, not a stop - elapsed time is kept and the button
reads Pause / Resume / Start depending on state.

Due dates:

Tasks gain an optional `dueDate` held as a plain "YYYY-MM-DD" calendar
day. Dates are never parsed with `new Date(str)`, which reads a bare
date as UTC midnight and lands a day early for anyone west of
Greenwich; src/utils/date.js builds and reads them from local parts.

- New DatePicker: a month grid popover with prev/next month, today and
  selection highlighting, Today / Tomorrow / +1 week shortcuts and a
  Clear action. Closes on Escape or an outside click.
- Set a due date when creating or editing a task, or inline from the
  task panel.
- Task rows show the due date, relative where it helps ("Today",
  "Tomorrow", "3d late"), in danger colour once overdue and accent on
  the day itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
