From ea7af1d496711e5c67e35d830658bca69784897b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:19:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Rank the information on a task row; let columns fill the
 width

With time tracking and due dates both landed, every row carried three
competing numbers in the same dim micro type, and the least actionable
of them was the most prominent.

- Elapsed time moves off the title line. It is a record, not a signal,
  so it is now the quietest value on the row and uses a compact form
  ("3h 12m") rather than a precise clock. A running timer still ticks
  to the second, in accent.
- The due date takes the title line, where urgency belongs, coloured
  only when it is today or overdue.
- Progress keeps the second line with its counter.
- The timer control moves to a reserved left gutter so the title no
  longer shifts on hover, and a finished task shows a check there.
- A finished task no longer shows a due date at all. Rendering "3d
  late" in red against completed work was both meaningless and
  alarming.
- Done rows collapse to a single line, with their time on the title
  line instead of a near-empty second row.
- Column headers surface open overdue work ("1 late") beside the count,
  so load is visible without opening anything.
- Columns flex between 300 and 460px instead of sitting at a fixed 300,
  which left roughly 600px of dead canvas on a 1600px screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014dtmom2BFbpLMj9Na8hSrG
