From 21f73df32c628a4948483d4fa4d238306d5cbf03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:30:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Add a work clock and task comments with attachments

Work clock:

New timeclock slice, separate from the per-task timers: clock in, clock
out, and a log of closed shifts. The header control shows the open shift
ticking, and its popover carries today's total, the clock in/out action
and recent shifts. `now` and ids are passed in so the reducers stay
pure, and the log is capped at 200 entries.

Persistence now covers both slices under separate keys, so a failure to
read one never costs the other, and each is only re-serialised when it
actually changed.

Comments:

Tasks carry an optional `comments` array. Each comment has a body,
timestamp and attachment metadata. URLs in the body are linkified on
render (http/https and bare www. only - anything else stays plain text).

Attachment bytes go to IndexedDB, not localStorage. localStorage holds
roughly 5MB for the whole origin and base64 inflates a file by about a
third, so a single photo would evict the saved boards; Redux keeps only
id, name, type and size. Images render as thumbnails from an object URL,
other files as download chips. Attach via the button, drag and drop, or
paste. Blobs are removed when a comment is deleted, when a task
carrying comments is deleted, and rolled back if a write fails part way.
Files over 10MB are refused with a message that explains why.

The task panel pairs Status and Due date rather than stacking two
labelled blocks, so adding comments doesn't push the panel longer than
it needs to be.

