From bd12c5ddf370d165f050e1a7e434c6fff142571b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:38:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Make the board usable on a phone

The hover-only controls were the real break: a touch screen has no
hover, so the start/pause timer on a task row, the delete control on a
comment and on a shift log entry were all unreachable on a phone. They
now use a `.reveal` class that hides them only where hover exists.

- Columns take 86vw and snap, so one fills the screen and a swipe moves
  cleanly to the next. They keep the flexible 300-460px behaviour from
  `md` up.
- Form controls render at 16px on touch via a new `touch:` variant.
  iOS Safari zooms the whole page when a focused input is smaller,
  which leaves the board scrolled and scaled. An earlier attempt used
  element selectors and lost to Tailwind's own class on specificity;
  a variant participates in the utilities layer and wins properly.
  Pointer devices keep the dense 13px type.
- Touch targets on the timer control and calendar days grow on touch
  and stay compact on desktop.
- The calendar becomes a bottom sheet on phones rather than a 232px
  popover that would overflow the right edge inside a two-column grid.
  The work-clock popover is likewise pinned within the viewport.
- The task panel gains a visible Close button, since "Esc to close"
  means nothing without a keyboard; the hint itself is desktop-only.
- Header respects the safe-area insets, and the clock collapses to its
  icon below 420px.

