From eca905ba9c8cfd98cb3a6ccced6d80471fe44c2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:46:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Replace the board with a date-grouped agenda

The columns-of-cards layout was the Kanban. Status was the layout, which
meant the only way to see what was due was to read every column. The
app now reads top to bottom, grouped by when work is due.

- Tasks from every status are flattened into one list and bucketed into
  Overdue, Today, Tomorrow, This week, Later and No date, sorted by due
  date within each group. Group headers stick while scrolling.
- Status becomes a property on the row - a dropdown - rather than a
  position on a board. Changing it dispatches the existing move action.
- Views in the sidebar: Today, Upcoming, All and Done, each with a
  count. On phones these become a chip row, since the sidebar is hidden.
- New `toggleTaskComplete` action and a tick control on every row. With
  no columns, done can no longer be inferred from position, and a task
  with no subtasks previously had no way to be completed at all.
  Completing stops the clock so finished work stops accruing time.
- The list is held to a readable measure instead of running edge to
  edge: it is read in sequence, not scanned sideways.
- First visit opens on All rather than Today when nothing has a due
  date, so a new board doesn't present an empty screen that reads as
  broken.

Column.jsx and Task.jsx are removed; AgendaRow and Agenda replace them.
Timers, the work clock, comments, attachments, due dates and
persistence all carry over unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014dtmom2BFbpLMj9Na8hSrG
